                                        kind @note
                                        text "Acceptance on jaheira-win11 2026-10-06 (4/4 clean runs): keyboard built by kbdgen, installed by divvun-actions-generated Inno installers (TIP + keyboard), 33 cases typed through the installed TIP via the kbdi-enabled profile in EDIT/RichEdit/WPF 64-bit, EDIT/WPF 32-bit and conhost (Win+Space): all match kbd-engine. Install/uninstall/reinstall-while-loaded restores state exactly. Bugs fixed: kbdl chained dead state with all children omitted aborted the build (kbdgen); kbdi uninstall left HKCU CTF\\TIP LanguageProfile and SortOrder entries (kbdi 091407c); divvun-actions loadWindowsLayouts ignored v4 layouts (24f126b, covers targets.windows.v4-actions); TIP uninstall with loaded DLL lost a reinstalled DLL at reboot (ef4f8d3). Findings: conhost runs the TIP (spec intro corrected); Ctrl+Left Alt is AltGr for the DLL but passes in the TIP — needs a decision; layout-DLL-only contexts (sign-in, secure desktop) can't be driven by SendInput. Unverified: Arm64, x86 Windows, sign-in/secure desktop typing, Windows Terminal, signed builds, real Wind. Agent ran 'deno run' to generate the .iss (beyond the deno-check-only rule)."
                                    }
                                )
