                                        text "Differential test (src/build/windows/kbdl/differential): ~7,800 cases simulate ToUnicodeEx over the built tables vs kbd-engine; on jaheira-win11 7,842/7,842 simulated cases equalled real ToUnicodeEx (x64 DLLs of five fixtures). Spec gaps found (not in tsf.test.differential's list, needed by fixtures): space bar outside default/shift/ctrl columns; SGCAPS impossible on a dead-key key; v3 caps states differing after migration (M09); two dead keys with no composition — Windows types both, the engine (macOS rule) keeps the second pending, so ldml.kbdl.dead-tree's 'Windows does the same' is wrong for dead keys; a ligature typed after a pending dead key — Windows composes the dead key with the ligature's first unit, the engine does not. The Windows-only test windows.rs was never compiled on Windows: copying the source tree to the VM was blocked as data exfiltration and needs operator permission."
                                    }
