                                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                        kind @note
                                        text "Verified on jaheira-win11: 70/70 typing checks (Win32 EDIT, RichEdit, WPF TextBox x64; EDIT, WPF x86): plain, dead keys, AltGr ligature and AltGr dead key, numpad decimal, commit on End, Backspace cancels pending dead key, text-rewriting transforms incl. surrogate pair (inject path in EDIT/RichEdit, range path in WPF). Layering proof: DLL alone ´ b = '´b', q' = \"q'\"; through the TIP b+U+0301 and ʠ. 36 COM entry points fault-injected -> E_UNEXPECTED + poisoned. Spec deviations to fold (node targets.windows.tsf.host-spec): tsf.keys.altgr — TSF never delivers WM_SYSKEYDOWN (Alt without Ctrl) to the key sink, so AltGr chords the engine would consume are registered as preserved keys (OnPreservedKey), with a 0xFF key sent after to suppress menu-bar activation (untested: no menu app); tsf.keys.identity — WPF passes lParam without scan code/extended flag, so scan code is recovered from the VK via the dummy layout (numpad Del with NumLock off behaves as Delete); OnKeyDown is only called for keys OnTestKeyDown ate, so commit-and-reset for passing keys happens in the test phase; EDIT/RichEdit report an extra text change after the service's own edits (counted and ignored); ActivateProfile's per-process flag switched the session-wide input method (driver restores previous); text inserted at a composition start can be absorbed — composition start is moved past it; a profile-switch sink was added (one CLSID, many profiles). Not verified: console/AppContainer hosts, password fields in real apps, secure mode/sign-in screen, menu-bar suppression, Shift Lock and B00 on real hardware, profile switching between two keyboards, Arm64/Arm64X, at_start. VM leftover: a first-run test DLL in admin's Temp is still loaded in explorer/SearchHost/msedgewebview2 and is scheduled for deletion at next restart."
                                    }
                                )
                            }

